    "https://vacancies.maastrichtuniversity.nl/job/Maastricht-Assistant-professor-position-in-Microeconomics-andor-Public-Economics/1373791057/": {
      "title": "Assistant professor position in Microeconomics and/or Public Economics",
      "description": "Assistant professor position in Microeconomics and/or Public Economics Job Details | Maastricht University Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile All jobs Working at Maastricht University Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Service Center All Job Type All Location All FTE min All FTE max All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Assistant professor position in Microeconomics and/or Public Economics Welcome to Maastricht University! The Department of Microeconomics and Public Economics (MPE) at the School of Business and Economics (SBE), Maastricht University, invites applications for an Assistant Professor position. We welcome candidates with a strong research profile in microeconomics, public economics, political economy, urban economics, inequality, health economics, behavioural economics, and/or experimental economics or related fields. Assistant professor position in Microeconomics and/or Public Economics Our goal: Strengthen and diversify our research and education in microeconomics and public economics – shaping knowledge that helps us understand and improve how economies and societies function. Your colleagues: You will join the vibrant, international academic community within the MPE department and the School of Business and Economics. MPE focuses on high-quality research in the above-mentioned fields. The department maintains strong links with other institutes and departments at Maastricht University and with leading international partners – offering you ample opportunity to collaborate and grow. Please visit the department’s website for more information. As Assistant Professor, you will contribute to research and education in the department. You are expected to strengthen and diversify the department’s research profile, publish in high-quality journals, and engage in external collaborations.  In addition to research, you are expected to contribute to teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. All teaching is conducted in English. We also expect you to apply for competitive research funding. We are committed to fostering a diverse, equitable, and inclusive academic environment. We warmly welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds and particularly encourage applications from women and other groups that are currently underrepresented in academia. What you bring We are interested in who you are and what you bring. Do you recognise yourself in this profile? Academic background – You hold a PhD in Economics or a related discipline. Strong research profile – You have a strong academic background, possibly already evidenced by publications in peer-reviewed journals. Funding potential – You can demonstrate the willingness or ability to secure external research funding. Teaching experience – You have experience in teaching at the university level, for example as the primary instructor or teaching assistant. Collaborative mindset – You value teamwork and collegiality, and you enjoy contributing to a positive, inclusive academic environment. You will help to create meaningful synergies and positive externalities within both the department and the School of Business and Economics. What we offer At Maastricht University, you’ll work in an international, open, and engaged environment. We offer: An 18 month contract with the prospect of a permanent contract based on mutual satisfaction. The position is graded in scale 11 according to UFO profile Assistant Professor, with corresponding salary based on experience with a gross monthly salary between €4.925,- and €6.682,- (based on full-time employment of 38 hours per week). You will also receive an 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus. 29 vacation days (based on full-time), four additional days off (Carnival Monday and Tuesday, Good Friday, and Liberation Day), and the possibility to accrue up to 12 extra days through compensation hours. Flexible working hours, a home office allowance, and the option to partially work from home. A solid pension plan via ABP, company fitness schemes, and access to various university sports facilities. Freedom and responsibility to shape your work independently and develop your ideas. A close-knit community of colleagues to collaborate and grow with. An inspiring work environment in the heart of Europe. Interested? For more information with respect to the position, please contact Prof.dr. Kirsten Rohde, Chair of the hiring committee (kirsten.rohde@maastrichtuniversity.nl). For more information on the MPE department see: https://www.maastrichtuniversity.nl/research/department-microeconomics-and-public-economics Or apply directly before: November 15th 2026 The application should include: Curriculum Vitae (CV) Motivation letter (max 1 page) At least one example of your research (e.g. job market paper) Short research statement outlining your research vision/plans (max. 2 pages) and how you see that fitting into and complementing the research at MPE. Teaching evaluations (if available) Two letters of reference, should be sent independently by the referees to lor_algec@maastrichtuniversity.nl . We kindly ask you to apply via our application portal and not via e-mail. The e-mail mentioned above is only used for the letter of references. This position is open to internal and external candidates. We look forward to getting to know you! About the School of Business and Economics (SBE) SBE is an international faculty for economics, business, and policy. We combine academic depth with societal engagement. Our education is small-scale and interactive. Our research focuses on themes such as sustainability, inclusion, and digital transformation. Together, we work on impactful solutions for the world of tomorrow. About Maastricht University At Maastricht University, we collaboratively seek solutions to help move the world forward. We do this with 23,300 students and 5,400 employees across 5 regional locations, 6 faculties, and more than 70 research institutes. We encourage you to push boundaries and discover new opportunities for yourself and the world around you. Together, we can find the answers for tomorrow. Maastricht University is committed to promoting and nurturing a diverse and inclusive community. We believe that diversity in our staff and student population contributes to the quality of research and education at UM, and we strive to enable this through inclusive policies and innovative projects led by teams of staff and students. We encourage applicants from all backgrounds to apply for this position. Job Type: Academic Faculty/Service Center: School of Business and Economics Closing date: 15-11-2026 FTE min: 1,0 FTE max: 1,0 Salary min: €4925,00 Salary max: €6682,00 ID job: 3786 Job Type: Academic Faculty/Service Center: School of Business and Economics Closing date: 15-11-2026 FTE min: 1,0 FTE max: 1,0 Salary min: €4925,00 Salary max: €6682,00 ID job: 3786 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://vacancies.maastrichtuniversity.nl/job/Maastricht-Assistant-Professor-in-Predictive-Brain-Processes/1374452157/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Predictive Brain Processes",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Predictive Brain Processes Job Details | Maastricht University Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile All jobs Working at Maastricht University Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Service Center All Job Type All Location All FTE min All FTE max All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Assistant Professor in Predictive Brain Processes Welcome to Maastricht University! How does the brain construct an adaptive interpretation of the world? How do sensory information, prior knowledge, expectations, goals and internal states interact to shape perception, learning and decision-making? At the Department of Cognitive Neuroscience of Maastricht University, we are looking for an Assistant Professor in Predictive Brain Processes who wants to develop an ambitious and independent research programme that advances our mechanistic understanding of how the brain anticipates, infers, learns and acts under uncertainty. Assistant Professor in Predictive Brain Processes Our goal: You will establish an independent and internationally visible research programme in predictive brain processes and contribute to the education programmes of the Faculty of Psychology and Neuroscience. Your colleagues: You will join the Cognitive Neuroscience (CN) department within the Faculty of Psychology and Neuroscience (FPN) at Maastricht University. CN currently consists of around 60 permanent staff members and approximately 70   temporary staff members, including PhD candidates and postdocs. We are a collaborative group investigating the neural processes underlying human cognitive functions, including perception, attention, emotion, memory, learning, language and neurocognitive development. CN combines different approaches to measuring and manipulating brain activity and overt behaviour, including MRI at 3T and 7T, EEG, psychophysics, non-invasive brain stimulation (NIBS) and neurofeedback. Experimental expertise comes together with methodological development and theoretical and computational approaches. Alongside fundamental research, our work also connects to applications such as brain-computer interfaces (BCIs) for people with locked-in syndrome, the treatment of depression and the remediation of dyslexia. What you do You will have the intellectual freedom to build an independent and internationally visible research programme in predictive and inferential brain processes. Your research may take an experimental, computational or theoretical approach. We are not committed to a single theoretical framework: we welcome research that develops, tests, compares, refines or challenges existing theories. Contributing to a deeper understanding of the computations and mechanisms underlying adaptive cognition, your research may focus on areas such as: Perception, learning and working memory Statistical and sequence learning Conscious experience Abstract and compositional representations Decision-making and sensorimotor control You may work in any sensory modality, across multiple modalities or in modality-general domains, using approaches such as psychophysics, eye-tracking, neuroimaging, non-invasive electrophysiology and computational modelling. We are particularly interested in formal, computational, biologically inspired, generative or neural-network models that advance theories of brain function. Alongside developing your research programme, you will: Develop collaborative research projects and pursue external research funding. Contribute to an open, supportive and inclusive research culture. Divide your time approximately 50/50 between research and teaching. Teach within the interdisciplinary BSc Brain Science, particularly in areas related to your expertise, such as cognitive and computational neuroscience, perception and cognition, mathematics, programming, modelling, artificial intelligence and data analysis. Contribute to the FPN Psychology bachelor’s and master’s programmes and, occasionally, programmes outside FPN. Supervise bachelor’s and master’s theses. Contribute to administrative responsibilities or committee work once you are settled in your role. Are you ready to set the course for the years ahead? Then we’d love to meet you. What you bring We’re not looking for checkboxes; we’re interested in who you are and what you bring. Do you recognize yourself in this? You: Have a PhD in (Cognitive) Psychology, (Computational) Neuroscience, Biomedical Sciences or Engineering, Artificial Intelligence or a related discipline. Have postdoctoral or equivalent research experience, with demonstrated research quality and a competitive publication record. Have strong theoretical, computational and/or experimental expertise relevant to the interplay between sensation and cognition and to predictive and inferential brain processes. Have demonstrated the ability, or clear potential, to acquire competitive research funding, individually or collaboratively. Have the potential to develop an independent and internationally visible research programme that complements and strengthens the department. We welcome research spanning behaviour and cognition, representations, algorithms, neural populations and circuits. Expertise in a particular sensory modality or research method is not required. Have relevant teaching experience and enthusiasm for further developing your teaching and thesis supervision. Are a collegial researcher who enjoys interdisciplinary team science. Have excellent English communication skills. Knowledge of Dutch is not required. What we offer At Maastricht University, you’ll work in an international, open, and engaged environment. We offer: A 12-month contract (1,0 fte) with the prospect of a permanent contract based on mutual satisfaction. A gross monthly salary between €4925,00 and €6682,00 (based on full-time employment of 38 hours per week). 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus. 29 vacation days (based on full-time), four additional days off (Carnival Monday and Tuesday, Good Friday, and Liberation Day), and the possibility to accrue up to 12 extra days through compensation hours. Flexible working hours, a home office allowance, and the option to work from home. Freedom and space to shape your work independently and develop your ideas. A close-knit community of colleagues to collaborate and grow with. A solid pension plan via ABP, company fitness schemes, and access to various university sports facilities. An inspiring work environment in the heart of Europe. About the Faculty of Psychology and Neuroscience (FPN) At FPN, we share a curiosity about the human brain and behaviour. Together with our students, we explore how our brains function and learn why we do what we do. We connect perspectives and contribute to living together in society. Interested? Want to know more about this position or what it’s like to work at our university? Reach out to Prof. dr. Federico De Martino at f.demartino@maastrichtuniversity.nl. The end date of the publication is 1 November 2026. Please upload the following documents to your application: CV Motivation letter that contains your ambition in relation to the mission of CN & FPN, research, leadership and teaching. (max. 2 A4 pages). Please at contact details of at least two references in the motivation letter. A clear research statement (max. 3 A4 pages) Apply now via the button below. We look forward to getting to know you! About Maastricht University At Maastricht University, we collaboratively seek solutions to help move the world forward. We do this with 23,300 students and 5,400 employees across 5 regional locations, 6 faculties, and more than 70 research institutes. We encourage you to push boundaries and discover new opportunities for yourself and the world around you. Together, we can find the answers for tomorrow. The vacancy is open for internal and external candidates. In case of equal qualifications, internal candidates will be prioritized. At Maastricht University, we prefer to contact potential candidates directly. We therefore kindly ask that no agencies or intermediaries submit offers or approaches. Maastricht University is committed to promoting and nurturing a diverse and inclusive community. We believe that diversity in our staff and student population contributes to the quality of research and education at UM, and strive to enable this through inclusive policies and innovative projects led by teams of staff and students. We encourage you to apply for this position. Job Type: Academic Faculty/Service Center: Faculty of Psychology and Neuroscience Closing date: 1-11-2026 FTE min: 1,0 FTE max: 1,0 Salary min: €4925,00 Salary max: €6682,00 ID job: 3831 Job Type: Academic Faculty/Service Center: Faculty of Psychology and Neuroscience Closing date: 1-11-2026 FTE min: 1,0 FTE max: 1,0 Salary min: €4925,00 Salary max: €6682,00 ID job: 3831 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
